# HackMyAgent suppressions. Each entry must state why the finding is not real.
# A suppression with no justification is indistinguishable from hiding a bug.

# ci/gitlab-ci-policy.yml:119 is a GitLab `rules:if` expression:
#     - if: '$CRYPTOSERVE_API_URL && $CRYPTOSERVE_API_KEY'
# It references two variables by NAME and contains no value. The credentials
# detector matches on the identifier rather than on an assigned secret, so it
# reports the opposite of what the line does: this is the recommended pattern
# for keeping keys out of source.
#
# Verified 2026-07-27 by independent grep for real credential formats across
# the whole tree (sk-ant-api, sk-proj-, AKIA, ghp_, npm_, PEM private keys).
# Only hits are PEM header assertions in tests and AWS's own published example
# key AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE in a documented release-smoke fixture.
#
# This is a false positive in our own scanner and is tracked for a fix in
# hackmyagent rather than left as a permanent suppression.
ci/gitlab-ci-policy.yml
